      "bdd.quiz.a": "A. The Outline runs 4 parameterized cases; the 4 separate Scenarios run 4 independent cases. Test counts are the same.",
      "bdd.quiz.b": "B. The Outline reuses one step-binding pass, the 4 Scenarios re-resolve bindings 4\xD7 \u2014 Outline is therefore meaningfully faster.",
      "bdd.quiz.c": "C. The Outline shares Background state across rows; 4 Scenarios each get a fresh Background \u2014 Outline tests are coupled.",
      "bdd.quiz.d": "D. The Outline can only run with a single discount code; 4 Scenarios can vary every step.",
      "bdd.quiz.correct": "Correct! Both forms produce the same number of independent test cases with identical isolation; the Outline is purely a syntactic convenience for parameterization.",
